## 1. Resolution of Prior Review Findings

1. **Idle turn clock & empty-mailbox yield (Resolved):**
   - [`MessageTurn`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/src/tasks/actor.rs#L648-L698) now initializes `began: None`, clears `began = None` in [`parked()`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/src/tasks/actor.rs#L669-L675) when `rx.poll_recv(cx)` returns `Pending`, and starts the turn clock via [`resumed()`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/src/tasks/actor.rs#L676-L678) (`self.began.get_or_insert_with(Instant::now)`) only when `rx.poll_recv(cx)` returns `Poll::Ready(Some(_))` ([`actor.rs:732-742`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/src/tasks/actor.rs#L732-L742)).
   - [`MessageTurn::after_message`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/src/tasks/actor.rs#L679-L697) immediately calls `self.parked()` and returns without calling `yield_now()` when `empty` (`rx.is_empty()`) is `true`. Covered by [`idle_time_is_excluded_and_an_empty_mailbox_needs_no_yield`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/src/tasks/actor.rs#L1859-L1874).

2. **Cancellation during batch yield (Resolved):**
   - [`run_actor`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/src/tasks/actor.rs#L760-L770) now rechecks `if cancellation_token.is_cancelled() { break; }` immediately after `turn.after_message(rx.is_empty()).await` before the next loop iteration can poll `rx.poll_recv(cx)`. Covered by the deterministic manual-poll regression test [`stop_during_batch_yield_does_not_execute_the_next_queued_message`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/src/tasks/actor.rs#L1876-L1924).

3. **Process-owned shard pool, detached helpers, cross-backend monitors, and blocking children (Resolved):**
   - [`registry()`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/rt/src/tasks/experimental.rs#L153-L156) now holds `OnceLock<Mutex<Option<Arc<Pool>>>>` instead of `Weak<Pool>`, so the last sharded actor stopping no longer drops the pool or calls `runtime.shutdown_background()` underneath detached `tokio::spawn` helpers, monitor waiter tasks, or `Backend::Blocking` children.
   - Non-`Async` backends (`Backend::Blocking` and `Backend::Thread`) acquire a conservative [`RuntimeLease`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/rt/src/tasks/experimental.rs#L184-L197) via [`lease_if_initialized()`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/rt/src/tasks/experimental.rs#L188-L197) in [`ActorRef::spawn`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/src/tasks/actor.rs#L583-L590) whenever the experimental pool exists.
   - Covered by [`detached_helper_and_blocking_child_outlive_parent_stop`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/tests/full_actor_shards.rs#L349-L373) and [`monitor_helper_survives_the_last_sharded_actor_stopping`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/tests/full_actor_shards.rs#L403-L442).

4. **Resource limit tests & `SPAWNED_EXPERIMENT_RUNTIME=current` (Resolved):**
   - `SPAWNED_EXPERIMENT_RUNTIME=current` is implemented in [`threads::block_on`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/rt/src/threads/mod.rs#L53-L57), giving `Backend::Thread` in `dedicated` mode the same `current_thread` Tokio runtime flavor as each shard worker.
   - [`descriptor_limit_is_scoped_to_children`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/tests/backend_resource_limits.rs#L82-L124) and [`descriptor_limit_child`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/tests/backend_resource_limits.rs#L128-L201) now test `"async"` (default `Backend::Async` control), `"sharded"` (warmed shard reactor reuse), `"dedicated"` (`Backend::Thread` with `current` failing to allocate a new reactor under `EMFILE`), and `"sharded-cold"` (cold shard initialization failing cleanly under `EMFILE` without poisoning [`registry()`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/rt/src/tasks/experimental.rs#L153-L156) and recovering once descriptors are released).
   - [`persistent_blocking_actors_queue_until_a_worker_is_released`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/tests/backend_resource_limits.rs#L33-L78) deterministically awaits both initial `started()` hooks and verifies the 3rd actor remains unstarted across a 25ms timeout before releasing a worker.

