## 2. Inspection of Shutdown, Registration & Lease Races

- **`actor.join()` vs. `shutdown_sharded()` lease release race — Sound:**
  - In [`ActorRef::spawn`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/src/tasks/actor.rs#L588-L601), `completion_tx.send(Some(reason))` fires just before `inner_future` returns and drops either [`Pool::spawn`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/rt/src/tasks/experimental.rs#L105-L110)'s `_lease` (for sharded `Backend::Async`) or `_borrowed_runtime` (for `Backend::Blocking` / `Backend::Thread`).
  - [`Pool::shutdown`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/rt/src/tasks/experimental.rs#L120-L133) holds `self.state.lock()` and waits on `self.idle.wait_timeout(state, remaining)` while `state.active != 0` *before* calling `state.senders.take()`. Thus, an observer thread that calls `actor.join().await` and immediately invokes `shutdown_sharded()` will wait for the worker to finish polling the wrapper future and drop `Lease` before closing `senders` or shutting down the shard runtimes.
- **`Pool::spawn` vs. `Pool::shutdown` registration serialization — Sound:**
  - [`Pool::spawn`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/rt/src/tasks/experimental.rs#L95-L104) checks `state.senders.as_ref()` and increments `state.active += 1` under the same `self.state` mutex acquisition.
  - Consequently, `Pool::shutdown` cannot observe `state.active == 0` and take `state.senders` while a `Pool::spawn` call is in the window between releasing `self.state` ([line 104](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/rt/src/tasks/experimental.rs#L104)) and calling `tx.send(...)` ([line 107](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/rt/src/tasks/experimental.rs#L107)). If `tx.send(...)` ever failed, dropping the unsent closure drops `lease` outside the lock and decrements `state.active`.
- **Self-join check vs. concurrent `shutdown()` — Sound:**
  - `worker_ids: Vec<thread::ThreadId>` is populated during [`Pool::new`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/rt/src/tasks/experimental.rs#L85) and is immutable afterward. [`Pool::shutdown`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/rt/src/tasks/experimental.rs#L114-L118) checks `self.worker_ids.contains(&thread::current().id())` before locking `self.state` or `self.workers`, so a call from a shard worker is rejected immediately even if another thread is concurrently joining workers in `self.workers.lock()`.
  - Two external threads calling `shutdown_sharded()` concurrently both synchronize on `self.workers.lock()` ([line 134](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/rt/src/tasks/experimental.rs#L134)), so the second caller does not return `Ok(())` until the first caller has finished joining all shard threads.
- **Partial initialization failure in `Pool::new` — Sound:**
  - If thread spawn or `Builder::new_current_thread().enable_all().build()` fails on shard $k > 0$, [`Pool::drop`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/rt/src/tasks/experimental.rs#L142-L151) takes `senders` and joins shards $0..k-1$, leaving `*registry` as `None` so subsequent initialization can succeed.

