## 3. Remaining Contract Violations vs. Disclosed Experimental Differences

### Remaining Contract Violation: `exit_reason()`, `ChildHandle::is_alive()`, and `ChildHandle::wait_exit_blocking()` on spawn/startup failure

When [`rt::experimental::spawn_sharded(inner_future)`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/src/tasks/actor.rs#L609-L614) returns `Err(error)` (either during cold initialization under FD exhaustion as in `sharded-cold`, or when `Actor::start()` is called after `shutdown_sharded()`), `inner_future` is dropped without ever running:
```rust
if let Err(error) = rt::experimental::spawn_sharded(inner_future) {
    actor_ref.cancellation_token.cancel();
    drop(MonitorCleanup(actor_ref.monitors.clone()));
    tracing::error!("Experimental shard startup failed: {error}");
}
return actor_ref;
```
Because `inner_future` owned `completion_tx` (initialized via `watch::channel(None)` at [`actor.rs:557`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/src/tasks/actor.rs#L557)), dropping `inner_future` closes `completion_tx` while the stored value in `completion_rx` is still `None` (the same also happens for `Backend::Thread` when `threads::block_on` panics at `build().unwrap()` before polling `inner_future`, as in `dedicated` under `EMFILE`).

While [`ActorRef::wait_exit`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/src/tasks/actor.rs#L501-L511) and [`ChildHandle::wait_exit_async`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/src/child_handle.rs#L162-L171) treat `rx.changed().await.is_err()` as `ExitReason::Kill`, the synchronous status and blocking-wait methods only inspect `rx.borrow().clone()`:
- [`ActorRef::exit_reason`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/src/tasks/actor.rs#L496-L498) (`self.completion_rx.borrow().clone()`) returns `None` permanently—even **after** `actor.wait_exit().await` has returned `ExitReason::Kill`.
- [`ChildHandle::exit_reason`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/src/child_handle.rs#L121-L126) returns `None` permanently, and [`ChildHandle::is_alive`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/src/child_handle.rs#L116-L118) (`self.exit_reason().is_none()`) returns **`true` permanently** for an actor that failed to start and has already terminated with `ExitReason::Kill`.
- [`ChildHandle::wait_exit_blocking`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/src/child_handle.rs#L212-L242) checks `if let Some(reason) = rx.borrow().clone() { return reason; }` for its fast path ([line 215](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/src/child_handle.rs#L215)). Because `rx.borrow()` remains `None`, the fast path is bypassed even after `wait_exit_async().await` has completed:
  - Calling `handle.wait_exit_blocking()` on a `current_thread` runtime (after `handle.wait_exit_async().await` already returned `ExitReason::Kill`) **panics** at [`child_handle.rs:234`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/src/child_handle.rs#L234) instead of taking the already-exited fast path.
  - Calling `handle.wait_exit_blocking()` from a non-runtime thread while FDs are still exhausted falls through to `spawned_rt::threads::block_on(wait)` ([`child_handle.rs:224`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/src/child_handle.rs#L224)), which attempts `Runtime::new().unwrap()` and **panics with `EMFILE`**.

*(Note: Either sending `Some(ExitReason::Kill)` on `completion_tx` before dropping it on startup failure, or falling back to `rx.has_changed().is_err().then_some(ExitReason::Kill)` in `exit_reason()`, would make `exit_reason()`, `is_alive()`, and `wait_exit_blocking()`'s fast path consistent with `wait_exit()`.)*

